.\" pymnifocus-query man page
.TH PYMNIFOCUS\-QUERY 1 "March 2026" "pymnifocus 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pymnifocus\-query \- query OmniFocus from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pymnifocus\-query
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ JSON_INPUT ]
.br
.I command
.B |
.B pymnifocus\-query
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pymnifocus\-query
is a command\-line tool for querying an OmniFocus database on macOS.
It supports both convenience flags for common queries and raw JSON input
using the same format as the MCP
.B query_omnifocus
tool.
.PP
OmniFocus must be running for this tool to function.
Communication is entirely local via OmniJS scripts executed through
.BR osascript (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Positional Arguments"
.TP
.I JSON_INPUT
A JSON query object passed as a positional argument.
Must contain at least an \fB"entity"\fR field.
If omitted and stdin is not a terminal, JSON is read from stdin.
.SS "Query Shortcuts"
.TP
.B \-\-inbox
Show inbox tasks.
.TP
.B \-\-flagged
Show flagged tasks.
.TP
.B \-\-overdue
Show overdue tasks.
.TP
.B \-\-due\-soon
Show tasks that are due soon.
.TP
.B \-\-available
Show available and next tasks.
.TP
.B \-\-blocked
Show blocked tasks.
.TP
.B \-\-today
Show tasks due today.
.TP
.BI \-\-due\-within " DAYS"
Show tasks due within
.I DAYS
days.
.TP
.BI \-\-planned\-within " DAYS"
Show tasks planned within
.I DAYS
days.
.TP
.BI \-\-project " NAME" "\fR,\fP " \-p " NAME"
Show tasks in the named project (partial, case\-insensitive match).
.TP
.BI \-\-tag " TAG" "\fR,\fP " \-t " TAG"
Show tasks with the given tag.
May be repeated to match multiple tags.
.TP
.B \-\-has\-note
Show tasks that have notes.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-note
Show tasks that do not have notes.
.SS "Query Options"
.TP
.BI \-\-entity " TYPE" "\fR,\fP " \-e " TYPE"
Entity type to query:
.BR tasks ", " projects ", or " folders .
Default:
.BR tasks .
.TP
.BI \-\-fields " FIELD" "\fR [\fPFIELD\fR ...]\fP,\fP " \-f " FIELD" "\fR [\fPFIELD\fR ...]\fP"
Specific fields to return in results.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N" "\fR,\fP " \-n " N"
Maximum number of results to return.
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " FIELD" "\fR,\fP " \-s " FIELD"
Sort results by field (e.g.\&
.BR dueDate ", " name ).
.TP
.BI \-\-sort\-order " DIR"
Sort direction:
.B asc
or
.BR desc .
.TP
.B \-\-completed
Include completed items in results.
.TP
.B \-\-summary
Return count only, without full item data.
.SS "Other Tools"
.TP
.B \-\-dump
Print a full database snapshot (tasks, projects, folders, tags).
.TP
.B \-\-tags
List all tags with hierarchy and task counts.
.TP
.B \-\-perspectives
List all available perspectives.
.SS "Output"
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output raw JSON instead of formatted text.
Useful for scripting and piping to other tools.
.SH EXAMPLES
Query using shorthand flags:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pymnifocus\-query \-\-overdue
pymnifocus\-query \-\-flagged \-\-sort dueDate
pymnifocus\-query \-\-inbox
pymnifocus\-query \-\-due\-within 7 \-\-limit 10
pymnifocus\-query \-\-project "Weekly Review"
pymnifocus\-query \-\-tag work \-\-tag urgent
pymnifocus\-query \-\-available \-\-summary
pymnifocus\-query \-\-today
.RE
.fi
.PP
Query using JSON input:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pymnifocus\-query '{"entity": "tasks", "filters": {"status": ["Overdue"]}}'
pymnifocus\-query '{"entity": "projects", "filters": {"status": ["Active"]}}'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Pipe JSON from stdin:
.PP
.nf
.RS
echo '{"entity": "tasks", "filters": {"flagged": true}}' | pymnifocus\-query
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use other tools:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pymnifocus\-query \-\-dump
pymnifocus\-query \-\-tags
pymnifocus\-query \-\-perspectives
.RE
.fi
.PP
Raw JSON output for scripting:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pymnifocus\-query \-\-overdue \-\-json
.RE
.fi
.SH JSON QUERY FORMAT
The JSON input accepts the same format as the MCP
.B query_omnifocus
tool:
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "entity": "tasks",
  "filters": {
    "flagged": true,
    "status": ["Overdue", "DueSoon"],
    "projectName": "Work",
    "tags": ["urgent"],
    "inbox": true,
    "dueWithin": 7,
    "dueOn": 0,
    "hasNote": true
  },
  "fields": ["id", "name", "dueDate"],
  "sortBy": "dueDate",
  "sortOrder": "asc",
  "limit": 50,
  "includeCompleted": false,
  "summary": false
}
.RE
.fi
.PP
Valid entity types are
.BR tasks ", " projects ", and " folders .
.PP
Task status values:
.BR Next ", " Available ", " Blocked ", " DueSoon ", " Overdue .
.br
Project status values:
.BR Active ", " OnHold ", " Done ", " Dropped .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid JSON, query failure, OmniFocus not running, etc.).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Requires macOS with OmniFocus installed and running.
The tool communicates with OmniFocus via OmniJS scripts executed through
.BR osascript (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pymnifocus\-server (1),
.BR osascript (1)
.PP
